.TH VIZIER 1 "October 2026" "Vizier" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vizier \- Linux dictation daemon and command-line client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vizier
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Vizier records a take and transcribes it with local Whisper or optional cloud
engines. The daemon owns recording and delivery; clients use a private Unix socket.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B daemon
Run the daemon in the foreground.
.TP
.B setup [\-\-no-portal] [\-\-autostart]
Probe desktop helpers, write starter configuration, and install a user service.
.TP
.B toggle
Start or stop a take.
.TP
.B cancel
Cancel the current take.
.TP
.B status
Show daemon and take state.
.TP
.B doctor
Report runtime and engine prerequisites. Missing prerequisites return exit 5.
.TP
.B last
Print the latest completed take's text.
.TP
.B history [\-\-limit N] [\-\-text]
List recent takes. Text is included only when requested.
.TP
.B config path|get|set mode MODE
Show configuration path or settings, or choose a configured mode.
.TP
.B key set NAME \-\-stdin
Read an optional provider key from standard input.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print binary and protocol versions.
.SH OPTIONS
.B \-\-json
returns a versioned JSON envelope.
.B \-\-help
prints command-specific help.
.SH FILES
Configuration: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/vizier (default ~/.config/vizier).
History and takes: $XDG_DATA_HOME/vizier (default ~/.local/share/vizier).
Socket: $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/vizier/vizier.sock.
.SH NOTES
Live cloud engines need libcurl 8.11 or later. Batch engines remain available
with older compatible curl versions. Desktop delivery needs a supported clipboard
and paste route; on a headless system the transcript remains in history.
